{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12294-say-a-freehold-is-the-dominant-supernatural-force-in-a-citym","id":12294,"title":"Say a Freehold is the dominant Supernatural force in a Citym","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-16T14:21:17-08:00","id":12294,"title":"Say a Freehold is the dominant Supernatural force in a Citym","content":"So say a Freehold is the dominant Supernatural Force in a city, this could be because its a small town an they are the only Supernatural Entity in large numbers there, or because the others have gotten eradicated or chased away in their own conflicts, or simply because Changelings outnumber the other factions. What are some good ideas for incorporating Non-changelings into a Freehold? In my games I've had large freeholds that have counted enchanted Humans, Fetches, Hobgoblins, Ghost slaves, and a small number of mages among its members. Its a good way to bolster Freehold numbers, particularly when humans/hobgoblins are allowed membership into a freehold you can boost its numbers from a few dozen with only Changelings to a few hundred. This can give a stronger sense of an actual community, particularly if their is a Freehold shared Hallow. And Titles like King carries more of a punch if your a king over hundreds of individuals rather then a couple dozen. One of the best parts is since lost Numbers don't correlate exactly to human population size you could have such a freehold in a smaller city or even a town or island. And Festivals can actually feel like festivals without needing to doop a bunch of drug addled mortals or slum it with only hobgoblins.<br /> <br /> But what are some ideas for how to incorporate others into a Freehold? And what are some interesting rules or customs for such a Freehold? And variations on how it would work with the various Court systems. Personally I think Changeling is uniquely suited to have the potential for this sort of setting, mayhaps because their Culture revolves around tolerance for waywards/vagabonds/homeless/mad, and combined with the sanctity and prevalence of Reliable Pact Magic, and the security/privacy of Hallows.<br /> <br /> So humor me here.<br /> Though I would be interested if you have something to say why a particular group would be especially dis inclined to join such a community.<br /> And feel free to suggest the minor Templates, or Fanmades as I am ignorant of a lot of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh and I think I'll fold this into here, but another idea I was going to start a thread on was this. What do you think about a group that has method for joining for all/most the Supernaturals through the Z/subsplat? So something that would say count as an Entitlement to Changelings, but has a branch that counts a Lodge for Werewolves, a Legacy for Mages, a Bloodline for Draculers, an Athanor for Prometheans. I guess for Hunters it would count as joining a Conspiracy, or maybe a compact, and for Geists it would be joining the Krewe of the Geists involved. And Mummies I guess would be part of the Cult attached to it, and I have no idea for the Demons I'm still learning about them.<br /> <br /> Once again humor me. :P<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> Okay let me list the major assumptions of this thread. If you read anything read this.<br /> <br /> The 1st point, this Freehold would be the major power in the area, so discussions of other supernaturals not joining and going to war is relatively moot as they would be in small numbers and likely just driven off or killed. Its about an Area where Changeling Culture is dominant and virtually the only game in town.<br /> <br /> The 2<sup>nd</sup> point is the area doesn\u2019t necessarily have to be a major city, it can even be a small town.<br /> <br /> The 3<sup>rd</sup> point is you have to make a Pledge of Loyalty to the Freehold to join, the particulars depends on what you want out of the game.<br /> <br /> The 4<sup>th</sup> point, is everything not under the control of the Freehold/the end of its territory would be a border march brim type area. You could run more of a squatters type population here, like the remaining supernaturals driven out of the premium areas of the city dwell here awaiting a pogrom, or just enjoying the riches that come with controlling an area with more freedom and less security.<br /> <br /> The 5<sup>th</sup> point is the Freehold would consist mainly of the City/Town itself along with prime areas it considers territory (like a state park or farm), and a communal Hallow with the size of five, hell it could be even larger like multiple hallows or a Rank 5 Hallow for each Court. The nearby Hedge would not be advisable to enter for non Changelings, but there would be various portals into the Hallow guarded by the freehold through the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","user":"Eldagusto","date":". 11-16-2013, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T15:03:21-08:00","id":12319,"title":"","content":"Just my two cents here. <br /> <br /> 1. Changelings are never going to accept other Supernaturals. The whole point of being a Changeling is that you are a paranoid, fearful wreck. Vampires aren't going to want to have any part of a group that literally harnesses the power of the Summer Sun. Mages would only want to study them, (case in point, Acanthus.) I don't really know nWoD Werewolves, but keep in mind that they shapeshift, and are not fully human, in that they are part spirit. Hunters...well maybe, depending on what kind. Prometheans, remember have the Disquiet/Wasteland thing going on, and add to that the fact that they literally feel more comfortable around fetches.<br /> <br /> 2. I would argue what you said about Changeling Culture. &quot;their Culture revolves around tolerance for waywards/vagabonds/homeless/mad.&quot; I really don't think this is correct at all. Anything not Human could be a spy for the Gentry. Anything supernatural could be a True Fae in exile. Freehold culture is close knit, sure, but also very exclusive. You have a layer of oaths, pledges, and whatnot enforcing peace. Changeling culture isn't tolerance, its xenophobia at its finest. Heck, Freeholds in different cities might not even communicate. <br /> <br /> 3. Now, since I'm sure you want a better answer, I'm going to target how I would bring in other Supernatural splats. I think you are most likely to see Mages, Vampires, and Created. <br /> <br /> 3a. Mages are students, first and foremost. Unless you get a really, really determined Acanthus, they aren't going to try to brave the Hedge after the first try. (Remember, Mages can't even walk on Trods. The Hedge eats their souls. No soul=No magic.) I would approach it on a Motley to Cabal basis. You aren't going to have totally open peace between the Mages and the Changelings, but you might have Changelings on a decent, cooperative basis with one or two Cabals. <br /> <br /> 3b. Vampires have connections. So do Changelings. A large Freehold is going to run into some agent of the Prince eventually. It really depends on how they meet. With a little luck, a business relationship is most likely. Also keep in mind that Changeling blood is addictive, (due to the Glamour) so that might be an issue. I do like the idea of a Beast finding a Gangrel and trying to befriend them. That has potential for Drama. <br /> <br /> 3c. Created are never going to be seen in numbers in a Freehold. Once Wasteland starts happening, they are going to be driven out or killed. What you might see, though, is a Changeling sponsored area for Created, staffed by Fetches. I'd call it a joint Spring/Winter operation, and have it focused on finding these &quot;half men&quot; and fixing them. (Side note, that would be a really cool Promethean Chronicle. Have them finish the Pilgrimage under the tutelage of someone who can never be human again. Very tragic.)<br /> <br /> 4. No. I don't think you could have an all encompassing Z splat, unless you depowered it immensely. Unless you want to go the route of each founder being a different Supernatural, you won't have the powers available. If you did it that way, I would have it focused on cross-species diplomacy. Give each member of the Embassy of Virtue bonuses to speaking to other Splats. <br /> <br /> Again, just my two cents!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/863-doctor-lazarus","name":"Doctor Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T15:16:18-08:00","id":12326,"title":"","content":"For the equivalent of an all encompassing Z-splat, the simplest and most elegant thing that springs to mind is a Pledge that non-Changelings can join in, making them beholden to certain individuals and responsibilities while at the same time giving them access to some cool, minor stuff.<br /> <br /> I reckon Sin-Eaters could work nicely. They tend not to interfere with other supernatural's stuff, would probably be able to fit in with the various Courts one way or another, and they tend to throw pretty damn fine parties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T15:44:29-08:00","id":12342,"title":"","content":"As it's written, from the start, most supernaturals don't know about other supernaturals except for rumors and what they've seen in movies. Even a Mage who awakens doesn't automatically know there's vampires and werewolves.<br /> The supernaturals that do know tend to know very little more than that. Werewolves and vampires exist, just like in the movies, but no idea about the Pure, Father Wolf, the various covenants and clans or the Beast.<br /> Changelings may be about tolerance (not sure if they are), but they're certainly about wariness. Trust doesn't come easy. A human can be a true fae in disguise, and while a few changelings may openly embrace vampires for some reason, an equal amount would worry that they are minions of the Keepers. Or at least a threat to their hidden lives. Vampires need food, after all, people food, unless you want them doped up on changelings all the time.<br /> <br /> As for others being disinclined, simply put everyone has their own agenda. Werewolves deal with a world that changelings won't understand. Vampires are princes of the night, and while a neonate may certainly bow and pledge before someone who calls themselves a king, older vampires wouldn't be likely to. Mages explore and dissect the world around them. Do you think changelings who've spent years being a slave to some alien being would appreciate being told that it was just some wild spirit or part of the fallen world?<br /> Even ignoring their own agendas, why would they put themselves beneath something else, something alien to them? It's one thing for a werewolf to accept another as alpha, it's another to accept another being entirely that can never appreciate the werewolf's lot in life and duty as Uratha, let alone a different one each season. And werewolves aren't even the most power hungry of splats. Would changelings agree to serve under a mage? An entire freehold of them? Cause if they didn't, he could just make them. Part of the whole reason the highest title vampires can hold is prince is because it would be so arrogant (and dangerous) for one be labelled king.<br /> <br /> All that said, if you want to run it there's nothing stopping you, I think you'd either have to ignore a lot of/all of the background of the other supernaturals and have a freehold that somehow manages to all be on the same page regarding what they want, but nothing's impossible.<br /> <br /> Also there's an entitlement, Lord Sages of the Unknown Reaches, they are the changelings that look into and make deals with other splats. I believe they can get some talens or some magic items from other splats. So they could be part of your tentpole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-16-2013, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T16:41:31-08:00","id":12366,"title":"","content":"Its almost like you didn't read my whole post... I said humor me here![IMG]file:///C:\\Users\\ELDAGU~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\msohtmlclip1\\ 01\\clip_image001.png[/IMG]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doctor Lazarus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12294-say-a-freehold-is-the-dominant-supernatural-force-in-a-citym?p=12319#post12319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just my two cents here.<br /> <br /> 1. Changelings are never going to accept other Supernaturals. The whole point of being a Changeling is that you are a paranoid, fearful wreck. Vampires aren't going to want to have any part of a group that literally harnesses the power of the Summer Sun. Mages would only want to study them, (case in point, Acanthus.) I don't really know nWoD Werewolves, but keep in mind that they shapeshift, and are not fully human, in that they are part spirit. Hunters...well maybe, depending on what kind. Prometheans, remember have the Disquiet/Wasteland thing going on, and add to that the fact that they literally feel more comfortable around fetches.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Saying Changelings are never going to accept other Supernaturals is Bunk, they shouldn't accept anyone much less other changelings. And Properly strict pacts have allowed them to form communities when they wouldn't have any reason to trust each other. But like I said in the beginning post the Changelings are the only strong supernatural presence in the city, and the city might not even be city but a small town, so anyone else are going to be a handful of locals, and the others are most likely exiles or refugees of some sort. Vampires often wouldn't have anything to with the values of other Covenants yet you still have Crone and Lancea Kindred in the same city. And many Vampires desire the sunlight again even if they can only experience it via proxy, and Ordo desire to conquer it one way or another. You\u2019re generalizing your groups far too much.<br /> Saying Mages only want to study them, that is an absurdly simplistic statement. First of all such a place would provide ample opportunities to observe and study supernatural phenomena. Mages are not just a bunch of dudes sitting in a tower reading books all day, they enjoy companionship , and even those that prefer to be left alone are free to do so under the aegis of being under a group designed for privacy and security. There is no particular reason why this would be anathema to a mage, and seeing as it is separated from the rule of the Diamond Order it is perfect for Apostates who do not wish to follow Seer or Diamond Mage rule.<br /> This fits just fine with Ghost Wolves, or any Foresaken who say want protection from the Pure that genocided all the Foresaken in their last home. Living in one spot is not ideal for Prometheans as part of the Pilgrimage involves travel. But having a home in the Hallow (which is immune to the Wasteland effect) is not to be disregarded, I\u2019m sure a lot of Nephri would love the simple luxury of having drinking water that didn\u2019t taste like crap. Not to mention the simple draw of Fetches who aren\u2019t bothered by disquiet. Finally those who achieved the new Dawn could end up anywhere, whether it\u2019s some crappy circus, or a palatial hollow.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doctor Lazarus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12294-say-a-freehold-is-the-dominant-supernatural-force-in-a-citym?p=12319#post12319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. I would argue what you said about Changeling Culture. &quot;their Culture revolves around tolerance for waywards/vagabonds/homeless/mad.&quot; I really don't think this is correct at all. Anything not Human could be a spy for the Gentry. Anything supernatural could be a True Fae in exile. Freehold culture is close knit, sure, but also very exclusive. You have a layer of oaths, pledges, and whatnot enforcing peace. Changeling culture isn't tolerance, its xenophobia at its finest. Heck, Freeholds in different cities might not even communicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their Culture does revolve around Paranoia and Tolerance. The majority of the lost return and have nothing until they take/make what is there\u2019s so all that join freeholds were wanderers/vagabonds at one point. And the books mention they have a large tolerance for crazy or mal-adjusted people (its in the book that discusses freeholds) because most Lost are essentially ex torture victims suffering from some form of post-traumatic stress disorder with an inclination for hallucinating. They don\u2019t imprison people, so they wouldn\u2019t have any freeholds just motleys if they went around killing every homeless or crazy lost they encounter. They are crazy Xenophobic, but, and this is a big but, a lot of that is handled because they can literally make magically binding pacts. The freeholds with the most problems with trust and Privateers are the ones that don\u2019t require a pledge to join. Those freeholds have more liberties and may even grow quicker but at the cost of security. The freehold discussed here is one that requires a loyalt pledge to join, thus ensuring at least a minimum security. And not every supernatural could be a True Fae, I don\u2019t know where you are getting this from but Exiled Fae would have a much easier time pretending to be one of the Lost. And this is an example setting where you may actually have Exiled in the outskirts of the community. I imagine a large freehold like this would have brim area that is more dangerous but less restricting.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doctor Lazarus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12294-say-a-freehold-is-the-dominant-supernatural-force-in-a-citym?p=12319#post12319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3a. Mages are students, first and foremost. Unless you get a really, really determined Acanthus, they aren't going to try to brave the Hedge after the first try. (Remember, Mages can't even walk on Trods. The Hedge eats their souls. No soul=No magic.) I would approach it on a Motley to Cabal basis. You aren't going to have totally open peace between the Mages and the Changelings, but you might have Changelings on a decent, cooperative basis with one or two Cabals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know why your even talking about getting lost in the hedge, half the freehold would be in the real world, and half would be the communal hallow (Size Five Hallows are the size of a whole village). All the mage has to do is not wander out the freehold. And you aren\u2019t going to have some sort of crazy mage war because like I said this is all based around the assumption that Changelings are the only supernatural in large numbers in the whole region, so a couple of mages to about a dozen on the extreme end of the spectrum. And you either make a pledge to join the freehold, or either keep to yourself and hide, or leave/be ejected or killed. Like I said the whole basis of this is Changelings are the majority of the area. It may even be a small area so you\u2019re not likely to a back up contigent of two Dozen Adamantine Arrows sent to reclaim Smallville when single remaining Arrow could just move to Metropolis, if you catch my drift.<br /> You live there and make a loyalty pledge, or you get the hell out of dodge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doctor Lazarus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12294-say-a-freehold-is-the-dominant-supernatural-force-in-a-citym?p=12319#post12319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> 3b. Vampires have connections. So do Changelings. A large Freehold is going to run into some agent of the Prince eventually. It really depends on how they meet. With a little luck, a business relationship is most likely. Also keep in mind that Changeling blood is addictive, (due to the Glamour) so that might be an issue. I do like the idea of a Beast finding a Gangrel and trying to befriend them. That has potential for Drama</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again the basic assumption is there is no Prince beyond a Changeling with that title, hell he may even have taken the title after scuffle turned into a war and the prince was beheaded, followed shortly by a quick Kindred Genocide. Seeing as how this is a potentially safe (relatively for a Kindred) haven for one of the Kindred, and it would be free from wider kindred politics this would be an ideal refuge for any Kindred trying to escape persecution. The only issue being if it\u2019s in a small town feeding would require very small numbers, maybe even like only two Kindred permitted to the Freehold of Smallville small. The other issue being, depending on the nature of the freehold they may need to swear off predation as part of their Pledge to join. That all depends on the mood of the Freehold you\u2019re going for, a no murdering mortals would be Utopia would differ from a Sun and Moon Court ruled so as you will to the ignorant mortals type of turf. But if there is room, and you\u2019re a kindred trying to not rape people of blood then this could be ideal, especially if addictive Bloodroot goblin fruit is found. Things like addiction to goblin fruit or changeling blood would also be quite desirable as it could be the source of much intrigue and even hidden cults, as potentially it could pass certain loyalty pledges, particularly if the pledge is lenient perhaps allowing certain actions when outside of the Freehold proper.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doctor Lazarus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12294-say-a-freehold-is-the-dominant-supernatural-force-in-a-citym?p=12319#post12319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 4. No. I don't think you could have an all encompassing Z splat, unless you depowered it immensely. Unless you want to go the route of each founder being a different Supernatural, you won't have the powers available. If you did it that way, I would have it focused on cross-species diplomacy. Give each member of the Embassy of Virtue bonuses to speaking to other Splats. </div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m just curious at how much you can play with the system before it breaks. I\u2019m not talking about everyone getting the same advantage, the major point of it is they are all part of the same organization, and can probably buy status in it, not really much to do with the power the individuals get from joining, though your suggestion of diplomacy is interesting. This basic concept could range to anything from an apocalypse cult, to a nazi driven Aryan Purity Conspiracy, to a Think Tank.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah let me clarify this Freehold would be the major power in the area, so discussions of other supernaturals not joining and going to war is relatively moot as they would be in small numbers and likely just driven off or killed.<br /> The 2<sup>nd</sup> point is the area doesn\u2019t necessarily have to be a major city, it can even be a small town.<br /> The 3<sup>rd</sup> point is you have to make a Pledge of Loyalty to the Freehold to join, the particulars depends on what you want out of the game.<br /> The 4<sup>th</sup> point, is everything not under the control of the Freehold/the end of its territory would be a border march brim type area. You could run more of a squatters type population here, like the remaining supernaturals driven out of the premium areas of the city dwell here awaiting a pogrom, or just enjoying the riches that come with controlling an area with more freedom and less security.<br /> The 5<sup>th</sup> point is the Freehold would consist mainly of the City/Town itself along with prime areas it considers territory (like a state park or farm), and a communal Hallow with the size of five, hell it could be even larger like multiple hallows or a Rank 5 Hallow for each Court. The nearby Hedge would not be advisable to enter for non Changelings, but there would be various portals into the Hallow guarded by the freehold through the city.<br /> <br /> <br /> But thanks for your two cents Lazarus I preciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T16:48:17-08:00","id":12370,"title":"","content":"Oh and what type of Court System do you think would be most interesting to have? I am saying a freehold of this size it would be interesting to say that at least some members of the known courts are around, but that doesn't mean you have to have all the Courts ruling. It could still be a basic rule of the Seasonal courts or the Directional, but it could also be some combination of the Courts like Day and Moon Court Queens Ruling with a Sun and Moon Court, or Dusk and Dawn Courts Plus Seasonal Courts... or why not all courts?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12294-say-a-freehold-is-the-dominant-supernatural-force-in-a-citym?p=12326#post12326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the equivalent of an all encompassing Z-splat, the simplest and most elegant thing that springs to mind is a Pledge that non-Changelings can join in, making them beholden to certain individuals and responsibilities while at the same time giving them access to some cool, minor stuff.<br /> <br /> I reckon Sin-Eaters could work nicely. They tend not to interfere with other supernatural's stuff, would probably be able to fit in with the various Courts one way or another, and they tend to throw pretty damn fine parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye not mention the fact that Sin-Eaters pretty much lack a large Global Culture so they are very much emphasizing a local culture/tradition sort of swing. With the Shades Contract their might even be an area of the Freehold built around preserving certain honored Dead, or they could start mapping and incorporating the immediate Underworld that lay beyond established Avernian Gates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T16:54:57-08:00","id":12374,"title":"","content":"A lot of this depends on the sort of game you want to run. What were you thinking? It could also be interesting to have the local Krewe's Mythos be something like a dark mirror of the Courts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T17:21:01-08:00","id":12384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12294-say-a-freehold-is-the-dominant-supernatural-force-in-a-citym?p=12342#post12342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it's written, from the start, most supernaturals don't know about other supernaturals except for rumors and what they've seen in movies. Even a Mage who awakens doesn't automatically know there's vampires and werewolves.<br /> The supernaturals that do know tend to know very little more than that. Werewolves and vampires exist, just like in the movies, but no idea about the Pure, Father Wolf, the various covenants and clans or the Beast.<br /> Changelings may be about tolerance (not sure if they are), but they're certainly about wariness. Trust doesn't come easy. A human can be a true fae in disguise, and while a few changelings may openly embrace vampires for some reason, an equal amount would worry that they are minions of the Keepers. Or at least a threat to their hidden lives. Vampires need food, after all, people food, unless you want them doped up on changelings all the time.<br /> <br /> As for others being disinclined, simply put everyone has their own agenda. Werewolves deal with a world that changelings won't understand. Vampires are princes of the night, and while a neonate may certainly bow and pledge before someone who calls themselves a king, older vampires wouldn't be likely to. Mages explore and dissect the world around them. Do you think changelings who've spent years being a slave to some alien being would appreciate being told that it was just some wild spirit or part of the fallen world?<br /> Even ignoring their own agendas, why would they put themselves beneath something else, something alien to them? It's one thing for a werewolf to accept another as alpha, it's another to accept another being entirely that can never appreciate the werewolf's lot in life and duty as Uratha, let alone a different one each season. And werewolves aren't even the most power hungry of splats. Would changelings agree to serve under a mage? An entire freehold of them? Cause if they didn't, he could just make them. Part of the whole reason the highest title vampires can hold is prince is because it would be so arrogant (and dangerous) for one be labelled king.<br /> <br /> All that said, if you want to run it there's nothing stopping you, I think you'd either have to ignore a lot of/all of the background of the other supernaturals and have a freehold that somehow manages to all be on the same page regarding what they want, but nothing's impossible.<br /> <br /> Also there's an entitlement, Lord Sages of the Unknown Reaches, they are the changelings that look into and make deals with other splats. I believe they can get some talens or some magic items from other splats. So they could be part of your tentpole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not tolerant as in peace love, everyone is equal, changeling culture is tolerant in that virtually everyone starts off as bottom of the barrel homeless refugees and they build communities where a lot of the people have mental and social disorders, and they learned not to be unnecessarily rude to the guy who never wears shoes and doesn't like to be touched. This is combined with the fact that they normally do not use imprisonment as it is an act causing degeneration of clarity and viewed as cruel and unusual.<br /> <br /> But as I mentioned, this not a situation where &quot;why would I join the Fairies I have my own courtly affairs of the Damn/Wise/Whatever,&quot; its a situation of if you weren't there to join the Freehold you wouldn't be there at all as the rest of your fellows are dead/left.<br /> <br /> <br /> So you join for the same reasons you would join most groups, its relatively safe, particularly if you are hunted or in exile. So in this way Changelings would kind have similar motives to the Unchained, particularly the Winter Court. If your not someone who would ever sign a community non-treason agreement you probably wouldn't join, but hell if you were like that why would even join a Vampire Court? Depending on the mood your going for the freehold the court rulers may have actual authority, or you may just be free to live there as long as you abide by the rules.<br /> <br /> But Honestly if your running from people trying to kill or enslave you, like the Unchained and Lost you may find it appealing to join. If you are a Mummy that achieved Apotheosis, and are hunted by the Judges and all their Arisen, yeah you have no native group you can turn to so once again join may be appealing. If you are a Ghost Wolf, or a pack of Foresaken and your entire state just lost big in the War against the Pure, yeah looking for refuge may be quite appealing. Same with any mage running from the Pentacle or Seers.<br /> <br /> One of the big draws for virtually all of the supernaturals is they have no one to talk to about their situation besides their own kind because they aren't allowed to tell mortals they exist. This is largely filled by a community like this as a Vampire can find some oathbound mortal to cry to, or even another ageless undead like the local Arisen Heretic. Prometheans are so desperately lonely anyone would do, and it would have a population of Fetches who don\u2019t hate you on sight, with a home where you don\u2019t ruin the Earth just by sleeping there. Yeah you could probably get stitch face to join just by the chance of meeting a girlfriend that won\u2019t try to lynch them because of disquiet. Many of the folks like Mages, Sineaters and some of the Lost can now go continue a mortal life by day with the guarantee that when they go back home they are just stone\u2019s throw from a community where they can be themselves.<br /> <br /> So really this is for a certain type of game, not every type of game. And Honestly I was designing it for a Changeling game, but it can fit for a changeling game with a member or two from another splat, or even a complete mixed group. It just spawned off the ideas I was tossing around for large freeholds, hence why the majority of the Freehold would either Changelings, or Humans/Fetches/Hobgoblins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T17:33:08-08:00","id":12389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12294-say-a-freehold-is-the-dominant-supernatural-force-in-a-citym?p=12374#post12374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of this depends on the sort of game you want to run. What were you thinking? It could also be interesting to have the local Krewe's Mythos be something like a dark mirror of the Courts</div> </div> </div> </div>Ideally yeah at least one of the krewes should build a mythos off of forming in the Freehold. Ceremonies are a type of magic that spreads culturally so you could start seeing them spread through the freehold even if it only counts as magic for the Sineaters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for Hunters, they would essentially fall under the human category as far as most anyone is concerned, except maybe for certain conspiracies like the Lucifuge and the Cheiron Group. But potentially if a Cell of Aegis Kai Doru joined they likely would be interested in the revelation that Token exist in large numbers in the Hedge, and many make it back to Earth or to Goblin Markets. It may raise a lot of fundamental questions about AKD philosophy when presented with a source of limitless relics. Some may have to figure what is more important about their philosophy the stockpiling of potentially useful items of power or regulating their flow into the mortal world.<br /> <br /> That is if they even are interested in joining the Freehold. Hell since hunters are human, and created in a reactionary manner Hunters could be one of the biggest threats to the Freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T17:45:19-08:00","id":12399,"title":"","content":"One thing I did want to address further. If you have an entire Freehold (lets say sixty Changelings) , versus a dozen Mages, the Mages will win every time. Mages can do <b>anything.</b> If you have 12, (lets say two Cabals of six) you've most likely got the whole spread of Arcana. Pledges don't mean much when the Acanthus invalidate them with a word, and with Forces and Death, and Life, that is most Changeling magic completely invalid. About all Changelings could do is retreat to the Hedge. <br /> <br /> I'm not trying to shut down your idea, but I am saying that it is very difficult to swing, unless you seriously gimp the motivations and driving forces behind the other Splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/863-doctor-lazarus","name":"Doctor Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T17:52:39-08:00","id":12403,"title":"","content":"I have a problem with the quotes here so pardon me not using them.<br /> <br /> Tolerance: One of the sample freeholds (Hacienda Suenos) takes in new changelings as slaves for five years. For five years after escaping the Hedge, you are forced to harvest and prepare cocaine for the others, who enjoy the profits of their cocaine empire. As written, the game isn't about tolerance.<br /> <br /> Join or die: Well this is kind of interesting in that a few of the splats would prefer to be alone, rather than among others. Changelings will never understand things the way Mages do, and now that a Mage is alone he can go and rifle through all their old master's research. Vampires aren't normally prey for some overarching threat, a lone vampire would be more likely to move to a vampire society or just make new vampires, wholly addicted to his power. Of course they could just join and bring the entire freehold under the Vinculum as well.<br /> <br /> Personally I don't really see fetches as part of a freehold, either, too many changelings would be way too eager to kill them for a wide variety of reasons. There's an entire entitlement based around killing fetches.<br /> <br /> It's clear you really want this scenario, however. So as I said you're going to have to ignore stuff like that. So you don't really need an explanation at all beyond 'everyone who doesn't join dies,' which is good enough, though you may have to flesh out that threat at some point.<br /> <br /> So your problem becomes how do I make everyone want to do it. In any group there's going to be people who don't like each other (for instance, some changelings might dislike the vampires who use disciplines and their Vitae to mentally enslave others). You had an idea for bloodlines and legacies. A sort of universal z-splat would be the way to do it. I'd suggest locking it to the area. The Silent Lodge, Silent Bloodline, the Legacy of Silent Hill, etc. It's not really an ancient conspiracy that's lasted across the world for centuries, it's just localized in this place. So you should probably spice up the place, think of some sort of historical precedent that would cause everyone to require the shelter of the freehold and work your way around that.<br /> <br /> You'll also have to figure out what the other splats do for the freehold. Even in the nicest of freeholds you have to participate, you have to give them something in exchange for everything they're giving you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T18:10:27-08:00","id":12410,"title":"","content":"Okay its ridiculous when you say you can predict what happens every time. Single mages have resulted in the deaths of over a dozen other mages before, and normal humans have successfully beaten mages, Slashers even has a fiction about a slasher picked off mages and people affected by magic. 60 changelings are 60 individuals with various powers that are rather unpredictable. You get say 5 Darkling Necromancers to haunt/gather intel from the mages, two dozen others using their social contacts/influence/allies combined with whatever other ones they need through the use of Vainglory to plague the mages infrastructure and frame them and their loved ones. Another couple dozen that can go through walls, or turn into pillars of flame, or literally throw trucks...<br /> <br /> 12 mages doesn't equal infinite manpower, not by a long shot. Doing magic properly takes a lot of time and preparation. Meanwhile while Changelings can't each do anything they can do magic they know cheaply and reliably.<br /> <br /> But yes I forgot to discuss the mages ability to alter pledges. I see this as a rather important part of the chronicle as they are pretty much the only beings able to so freely effect pledges. This can either be an unconfirmed secret in the freehold, or they can ply their trade at an insanely high price in secret at the brim. Or you can just run that Mages are specifically not allowed in or are hunted by down because of their history Oathbending for the freehold, nearly destroying everything. But once again I see it as only a handful of mages with certain power players in the Freehold aware of the potential of Fate Magic to alter pledges.<br /> <br /> But 60 changelings would be the low end of the spectrum against 12 mages the high end of their spectrum for this scenario. If there were only 60 changelings I would lower the amount of mages to 2-4. The high end of the Changeling population I'm talking about here well over a hundred. Miami after all I believe had 200 changelings. And I'm thinking of their being at least 150% humans as part of the freehold if not 300% or 400% if there was a trend of people bringing in their entire families, or a sizeable amount of social players like Fairests with a retinue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T19:46:07-08:00","id":12453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12294-say-a-freehold-is-the-dominant-supernatural-force-in-a-citym?p=12410#post12410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But 60 changelings would be the low end of the spectrum against 12 mages the high end of their spectrum for this scenario. If there were only 60 changelings I would lower the amount of mages to 2-4. The high end of the Changeling population I'm talking about here well over a hundred. Miami after all I believe had 200 changelings. And I'm thinking of their being at least 150% humans as part of the freehold if not 300% or 400% if there was a trend of people bringing in their entire families, or a sizeable amount of social players like Fairests with a retinue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting these numbers for Mages? <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?591295-Mage-the-Awakening-The-Man-Comes-Around\" target=\"_blank\">DaveB's Las Vegas setting</a> has on the order of 45-80 pentacle mages just in the local Concilium. That's not including allies those mages might have from out-of-town. Then there's other mage factions such as Banishers, Apostates, Nephandi, and Seers of the Throne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T21:04:39-08:00","id":12479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12294-say-a-freehold-is-the-dominant-supernatural-force-in-a-citym?p=12453#post12453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are you getting these numbers for Mages? <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?591295-Mage-the-Awakening-The-Man-Comes-Around\" target=\"_blank\">DaveB's Las Vegas setting</a> has on the order of 45-80 pentacle mages just in the local Concilium. That's not including allies those mages might have from out-of-town. Then there's other mage factions such as Banishers, Apostates, Nephandi, and Seers of the Throne.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay read the thread and you will get the answers. I specifically said a situation where most if not all the other supernaturals have been wiped out in the area, along with it potentially being not a major city (so a place of 100 or 200k not over a million). Along with it being a large changeling freehold, because changeling freeholds are not dependent on the size of the population but rather on the amount of trods in the area. So I'm saying for this setting less then a Dozen mages exist in the Freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T00:16:20-08:00","id":12558,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of good things have been said and I'll try and put down what I think and hopefully not repeat too much of what has already said...<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires:</b> As a rule they don't like other splats (unless they can exploit them with impunity) because they are big reminder they are not necessarily on the top of the metaphysical food chain. That being said they're not dumb. If a Prince is confronted with a Freehold that has a significant numbers and said freehold has/is cementing its power/ties in the mortal side of things, they are more likely to try and come to some sort of arrangement. Any conflict of any size could easily breach the Marsquarade. <br /> <br /> <b>Invictus</b>: If they have to they will go for polite, civil and at arms-length. They will make sure everyone else knows the Freeholders are off limits and what establishment they are not allowed to go within 500 feet. And they would make sure every other vamp in town knows anyone trying to make a deal with the Ling's without the Invictus present would be executed.<br /> <b>Ordo Dracul:</b> The Ordo would be the most likely to actively seek out and establish a relationship. A very tit-for-tat one based on occult knowledge, but some sort of agreement none the less.<br /> <b>Crone:</b> I think the Crone would have the same interest as the Ordo.<br /> <b>LS:</b> They would likely have a problem with the Changelings and would tell their flocks to stay away for any number of reasons. Some of their more militant groups might even try killing changelings for being demons or tempters and what not.<br /> <b>Carthians</b>: Somewhere between the Invictus and Ordo I think? I don't play Carthian all that much so I won't speculate.<br /> <br /> Where do they fit in, in this Freehold? Not a heck of a lot. No one likes being on the menu so Lings wont' want them around all that much. Spies, informants? They definately fill the roll of 'allies' and 'contacts'. Daevas might try partying it up with Springers and Autumn might have some sort of deal with the Ordo but generally the two would stay apart. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mages</b>: As many have said the Mages will be very very very..very very interested in Changelings. I can see individual cabals forming agreements with a big Freehold to avoid potential conflicts. Or the Seasonal Heads would meet with the Hierach and say &quot;Here is a list where we don't want to see your people, give us a similar list and we'll stay out of each other's hair.&quot; What it comes down to is numbers. If the mages are outnumbered they will eventually toe whatever line the Lings give them. Yes mages are powerful. But if the mages are caught off guard or its 12 on 50, the mages will loose. They'll take a bunch of Ling with them but they will loose eventually. <br /> <br /> Where do mages fit in this freehold? Similar to vampires but because of the sheer power of individual mages Lings would be skittish. If they aren't too pushy or rude you could easily have a situation where tokens and enchanted items could be commissioned back and forth. The more artist and scholarly minded mages and lings could get a long as long as boundaries are not crossed. <br /> <br /> Werewolves: I don't play WtF so the only realistic way I see it going down is 'Good fences make good neighbors.'<br /> <br /> Fetches: All I can say is what everything changeling I've played would say. Ehem. &quot;KIll it. Kill it fire. Kill it with bullets. Kill it trained attack dolphines. Kill it with green eggs and ham.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hunters: I can see it to some degree. Largely depends on the mentality of the Hunter. If he's on a crusade to fight 'the darkness' it probably won't work out. If they are part of the Thule or the Union, an amicable arrangement could be reached. Conspiracies...not so much. What happens if TFV finds out there's a Freehold that is 60+ and is actively trying to assert it's will over all the monsters and hunters in the city? What's to stop TFV from wondering if these Lings aren't trying to do that in city hall or sending people they've influenced to the state capital or DC? Cheiron might decide to send a whole mess of retrieval teams in while the picking is good. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T12:24:13-08:00","id":12873,"title":"","content":"It has always seemed to me that if there are enough supernaturals in a given place, they will inevitably run into one another. They might not understand much about each other, but glimpsing each other's otherworldly aspects becomes more likely with every meeting. Some groups could choose to stay away from each other, others might have truces, and yet others could try to kill each other on sight. Part of that will have to do with the history and rumors of the area.<br /> <br /> Depending on their current standing, supernatural groups do not necessarily have to be automatically antagonistic to each other. It depends on threats, resources, leadership, and the like. The Lord Sages of the Unknown Reaches are already in the books to act as a possible bridge between splats, but any cross-splat group would have would likely confer mostly social and knowledge-based benefits.<br /> <br /> Since you want this to happen, I suggest you go by splat and determine a few things:<br /> Population: Who's left of that type in the area?<br /> Recent threats: What's hurt them lately?<br /> Which other supernatural types they know of: Do they already know of other splats?<br /> Attitude toward other supernaturals: For whichever splat they know well enough to form an opinion about, give them a default attitude as per Damnation City pg. 156. Future meetings/deals/conflicts will modify that rating up or down the scale, depending on how they work out.<br /> <br /> This will set up the default way that the supernaturals talk about and treat each other, which will influence the player characters - but it won't (and shouldn't) define how the PCs ultimately feel toward other types. Their own experiences will determine that, and if they decide they hate the way the freehold bullies everyone into joining and decide to work against it, that is their prerogative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":227,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","user":"KismetRose","date":". 11-17-2013, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T12:03:15-08:00","id":15509,"title":"","content":"My thoughts for general trends:<br /> <br /> Vampires: Changelings and vampires are not likely to get along.<br /> <br /> This is just a flat statement of fact. Vampires are controlling, inhuman and dangerous in a way that is likely to evoke memories of the Gentry, but without the world-shaping powers that keeping changelings from killing the Gentry. On the flip side, changelings have hallucinogenic blood and lethal powers. If a vampire makes a pact with a local freehold, it will be entirely on an individual level, and there's no real &quot;this is how it's likely to shake out&quot; that can be drawn up.<br /> <br /> Werewolves: Changelings and the Forsaken are much more likely to get along, from what I know of Werewolf. Both have similar goals - protecting themselves and their people from dangerous creatures that live outside the world - and both tend to place strong cultural emphasis on honor and loyalty. I can see information-sharing pacts between urban changelings and rural werewolves going a long way, with both sides calling the other in when particularly large problems start to form, and a werewolf pack could attach itself to just about any Court (except maybe Winter) without too much trouble.<br /> <br /> Mages: Other people covered this pretty well, I think!<br /> <br /> Prometheans: As I understand it, changelings have no resistance to the Wasteland, and Prometheans are uncomfortably reminiscent of fetches. I can't see it ending well.<br /> <br /> Hunters: In theory, a moral freehold would be strong allies to a hunter cell; both sides are alert for dangerous monsters, and changelings know better than most people how dangerous the Wyrd can be. Plus, a changeling without magic isn't generally in trouble inherently (there's no real penalty for being out of Glamour), and they don't hurt the people that they draw Glamour from, so they are a &quot;safe&quot; supernatural group.<br /> <br /> In practice, it's going to depend heavily on the conspiracy and the freehold. If the local changelings are basically benign, they could make common cause with TFV, or the Loyalists of Thule, or the Union. They probably get along pretty well with the Lucifuge, who understand what it is to be both mortal and supernatural at once. Maybe they could work with the Malleus Maleficarnum, if they can prove they are victims of the supernatural, rather than agents, or the Agnis Kai Doru could make common cause with a more reactionary, Bridge-Burning freehold.<br /> <br /> If the freehold is actively meddling and doing damage, that's less likely. If the Hunters are determined to drag them out into the light (a la Network Zero), it's equally unlikely. If it's the Cheiron Group, not a chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Remember - popcorn can feel pain.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1195-frivyeti","name":"FrivYeti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:40:31-08:00","id":15591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doctor Lazarus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12294-say-a-freehold-is-the-dominant-supernatural-force-in-a-citym?p=12319#post12319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Changelings are never going to accept other Supernaturals. The whole point of being a Changeling is that you are a paranoid, fearful wreck. Vampires aren't going to want to have any part of a group that literally harnesses the power of the Summer Sun. Mages would only want to study them, (case in point, Acanthus.) I don't really know nWoD Werewolves, but keep in mind that they shapeshift, and are not fully human, in that they are part spirit. Hunters...well maybe, depending on what kind. Prometheans, remember have the Disquiet/Wasteland thing going on, and add to that the fact that they literally feel more comfortable around fetches.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could have sworn the books suggested that many Lings think that some of the &quot;Other Supernaturals&quot; are just particularly addled Ling's don't they? I seem to remember a common perception being that Vampires were some kind of cousin to Darklings.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img835/1264/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Do you see over yonder, friend Sancho, thirty or forty hulking giants? I intend to do battle with them and slay them.&quot;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/441-nighttrace","name":"NightTrace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar441_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:43:06-08:00","id":15595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NightTrace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12294-say-a-freehold-is-the-dominant-supernatural-force-in-a-citym?p=15591#post15591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could have sworn the books suggested that many Lings think that some of the &quot;Other Supernaturals&quot; are just particularly addled Ling's don't they? I seem to remember a common perception being that Vampires were some kind of cousin to Darklings.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do recall this mentioned in the Lost. This was indeed the case in Dreaming as well, where they called them Prodigals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T14:48:06-08:00","id":15640,"title":"","content":"They have a lot of theories about different supernaturals. One for vampires is that they're descended from fetches, or from someone with a powerful contract with blood. There's an entitlement I may have mentioned earlier in the thread (Lord Sages of the Unknown Reaches) who explore and deal with other supernaturals and tend to know more, but any theories do not extend to the entire splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T14:56:40-08:00","id":15645,"title":"","content":"I wrote a version of San Francisco where the Freehold was the overarching power structure and the rest of the supernaturals pledged into the Freehold. This was because the fog opened gates into the Hedge and thus Changelings were the ones best equipped to deal with the Bay Area. I never got to run this campaign, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T13:53:45-08:00","id":84210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrivYeti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12294-say-a-freehold-is-the-dominant-supernatural-force-in-a-citym?p=15509#post15509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts for general trends:<br /> <br /> Vampires: Changelings and vampires are not likely to get along.<br /> <br /> This is just a flat statement of fact. Vampires are controlling, inhuman and dangerous in a way that is likely to evoke memories of the Gentry, but without the world-shaping powers that keeping changelings from killing the Gentry. On the flip side, changelings have hallucinogenic blood and lethal powers. If a vampire makes a pact with a local freehold, it will be entirely on an individual level, and there's no real &quot;this is how it's likely to shake out&quot; that can be drawn up.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have seen this kind of sentiment before and I'm not so sure i agree. One of the things that i noticed (from my interpretation of the books anyway) is that you can count on Vampires to look out for themselves and in many cases, seek power. between the ability to grant all manner of mortal power and resources and the ability that several of the older, socially inclined vampires have at negotiating, i could see a case made for them wanting to deal on a large scale.<br /> <br /> and similarly The changelings cant possibly be expected to trust the vampires which is almost what pledges are for. and what you can obtain by getting the better end of a bargain with a vampire could be pretty tempting for a significant portion of the lost.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1445-elesho","name":"elesho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T10:42:12-08:00","id":84709,"title":"","content":"Some rather immoral Changelings could have a deal going to supply the local Vampires with food, then harvest the Fear from those poor souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T01:52:54-07:00","id":112489,"title":"","content":"the basic premis could work but there would be a lot of &quot;if&quot;'s involved. <br /> <br /> if the setting is a major city there would be a sizable vampire population to contend with. or if not something really really bad happened to them and the survivors have no choice but to swear fealty to the freehold. Perhaps a True Fae came in a mopped the floor with the blood suckers, (considereing the True Fae stats and basic Invulnerablity even in the material world thats not entirely unfeasable). if the setting is a small town, there would be a substantially smaller vampire population to begin with and making nice with the local fae courts is just eaiser than dealing with a city full of competition for blood. <br /> <br /> werewolves are a bit trickier. despite apperances, the Lost and the Uratha are not friends. Changelings are otherworldly weirdos who eat emotions and Uratha are tempremental furry death machines. Both sides are relentless hunted and thus prone to paranoia. furthermore the Uratha deal primarily with spirits, not True Fae, both are very alien and almost unknowable to the other. if the changeling courts had something to offer the Uratha such as tactical advantage over the pure by using guides throw the hedge to set up ambushes, supply of goblin fruits, and other such in exchange for having that furry death rage pointed toward the gentry on occasion, even better. it probly would cover more along the lines of alliance between sovereign states rather than fealty of vassal to liege.<br /> <br /> Mages are the easiest to incorporate, just have one survivor of going into the hedge and seeing what a horrible idea it really really is be in charge of his lessers and you solved the &quot;what you've been to Arcadia can you take me?!&quot; dilemma. haveing a a free hold at your back when the servants of the exachs come calling is going to come in handy.<br /> <br /> Prometheans, i'd say are probobly better off not being included in this grand expirement on the account of the disquiet which i don't know if its turned off in the hedge or not (if not definiitly don't use them that place is scary enough and as hollows are by nature apart of the hedge...) furthermore the promethan pilgrimage is designed to make the character human, and chagnelings for all their sad stories and memories are most certainly not. let the poor guy stash his stuff there as he moves on in exchange for comeing to defend the freehold when called upon. keeps them mobile and solves any and all problems with the disquiet.<br /> <br /> fetches are not created by changelings and are not by nature friendly to changelings. they are artifical simulacrum that are designed to steal a changeling's identity. the only soul they have is a maybe a little bit of the changeling's that their keeper scrapped off the thorns and stuffed into a scarecrow made of dried leaves and rabbit organs. if you would like the other critters to be a part of this that's cool, but Fetches are way too dangerous by nature for a freehold to keep around and a really, really painful insult to changelings that they are unlikely to forgive.<br /> <br /> likewise don't try to throw hunters into the mix, this place is already a powder keg just to due to being a motley crux of the various wod critters put together under the same roof and answering to the maddest of all their hatters. throw in a person who's sole purpose in life is to kill these things and it will just explode in your face.<br /> <br /> a giest should be fine here and there, especially when paired up with gravewrights. there shouldn't be too much to get involved so long as both parties agree as to what's what and how things should be done.<br /> <br /> just remember if your going to use these things in your chronicle don't gloss over what they are just for the novelty of having them there, a vampire is fundamentally a vampire and werewolf is a nine foot tall hulking engine of furry Apocalypse (pun totally intended). a powerful free hold is could make it work but they are going to have to step EXTRA lively if they want to keep the whole thing from blowing up in everyboies faces. have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T07:48:53-07:00","id":112634,"title":"","content":"Well, a few thoughts -<br /> <br /> 1) One, weaken the Veil between supernaturals. A vampire can recognize a changeling on sight, as he would another vampire. Changelings can see Vampire, etc writ all over him. Same with mages, prommies, demons, whatever. This makes interaction between various races easier. Strengthening the Mask, Obfuscate 2, aura manipulation, etc would hide the supernatural in question, but its a deliberate act on the part of the supernatural (except demons, but they specialize in looking like humans). <br /> <br /> 2) Vampires tend to be looked down upon by most everyone, and not because they're weak, but because I find that they're the most evil of splats - they're cannibalistic by nature, something that most other groups have rules against - killing/eating people for mana/essence is bad. Enslaving people is bad. Blood magics to live forever is bad. Vampires keep herds, brainwash people, and often inflict pain and addiction as the Beast rides their emotion. To a changeling's perspective, this very Gentry-like behavior. There should be a good set up to keep vampires in check. Maybe they're a guilty pleasure for some 'lings, or similar. Maybe there's corrupt 'lings in power who trade with the vampires. <br /> <br /> Mummies are probably the only splat that can match Kindred for being a highly evil splat. You're a servant to an evil necromancer who feeds off suffering and wants to take over the world, and pushes you in that direction. Your magic involves working with the dead and pain, and you, by your very nature and presence, brainwash cultists. A lot of the same problem with vampires, but coupled with religious zealotry. If vampires would be a racial equivalent to privateers, then the mummies would be loyalists.<br /> <br /> 3) Werewolves, Sin-Eaters, and Unchained tend to be focused on their spiritual antagonists. As long as they can do their job, and don't ruin territories, I suspect that there's no reason for them to not get along, and more than a few reasons to do get along (pledges for power not-with-standing). There's a bit of an issue with Werewolves and spirits, and how it interacts with some Contracts (notably, things like Contracts of Communion) and goblin vows, which could also be interesting. Darklings and some autumn get along with ghosts, so there's already precedent for that. <br /> <br /> 4) Demons... demons probably just hide from 'lings as it is, or make deals. Really, so could angels, so its problematic for demons in any case. Demons, due to how the war against their angelic opponents run, tend to need to have Covers that involve illegal and criminal activities, including gun running and human trafficking. Idealistic demons don't last, and they all do some very nasty things in the name of their war against God. That said, its not so different from the Changeling's wars against the Others, so there is a lot to hold in common there, once you get past different ideas of what hell means to each other, and that the big difference between God and Gentry is that one is emotionless, and the other is highly emotional. Both are still psychopathic powerful entities that can't empathize with humans and see them as toys/parts. <br /> <br /> 5) Mages and hunters are unique of races, in that they actively want to seek out other supernaturals. Mages to study so they can gain Arcane Experience from mysteries, hunters because they have a whole competition with keeping supernaturals from preying on humans - hunters and summers would get along, I suspect, while the more extreme hunters would more likely work with bridge burners. <br /> <br /> 6) Prometheans are rare as it is, encourage being abused, and run away. I can't see any of them wanting to stick around for long in any case, given the whole Pilgrimage, so discussing them, without first talking about rule changes for crossover, is an issue. <br /> <br /> 7) The Chicago has a small paragraph or three about what would happen if one supernatural ruled over others (two others, point in case). A vampire court dominating werewolves and mages, for instance, would have spirits chained in Elysium as guardians, and mage spells protecting the prince and his favorites. Think about what each supernatural could bring or benefit the Fae with. Spirits, magic relics/spells, trade in the taboo, communing with lost relatives, gadgets, etc. Giving each a subservient role (at least on the surface) in the city can help flesh your city out, and why the races in question just haven't been entirely driven out, or whatever. <br /> <br /> 8) Have fun! Sounds like a blast!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T09:42:21-07:00","id":114142,"title":"","content":"The first thought that comes to mind is that these changelings would probably do extremely well at goblin markets, and may even have an ongoing or regularly recurring goblin market in the freehold. Vampire blood, werewolf fangs and mage tears would all probably be very valuable at the market, to say nothing of more esoteric energies like raw plasm or bottled pyros. Of course, this wouldn't all be given to changelings for free but it would definitely give the town a lively magical economy. as for specifics:<br /> <br /> I don't know vampire too well, but I suspect that there would be a bit of friction with the more ambitious vampires who wish they could have more power and the changelings who know vampires can sometimes get a little\u2026 fae-like. that said, I think the ordo dracul would get on pretty well with the autumn court, and possibly the circle of the crone. the carthians would probably also appreciate the novelty of the changeling power structure, though honestly I'm not sure the carthians and invictus would really feature too prominently in the game since they're very much political entities and the changelings are the ones who hold the power.<br /> <br /> Werewolves I see falling into a sort of symbiotic relationship with the changelings. the emotion influencing powers of changelings and the way they feed can probably mess with the spiritual side of things sometimes but I imagine if they consult the werewolves they could turn those same habits toward making a healthier spiritual environment. in return, we have werewolves patrolling the freehold. having werewolves as backup when a bunch of privateers or even a fairy appears is in no way a bad thing.<br /> <br /> Mages, once they get past the &quot;can I go to arcadia&quot; stage and changelings get over any lingering suspicions they may have toward mages (depending on how mages act and are viewed the way you run them), would have a blast. The hedge, in small doses and with a changeling guide, is like a theme park for mages, particularly if they can go to some of the more mysterious places there. I cross mage and changeling plots a lot in my games (even had a mage who was taken by a keeper and awakened in arcadia) and once a mutual trust is established their strengths compliment each other extremely well and on a thematic level they benefit from being two of the most overtly fantastic things in the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> Prometheans would probably need to live on the fringes of society, though that's nothing new to them. They'd be able to work with the freehold and they may even be afforded some hollows in return where they can take up permanent residence without causing a wasteland, which would probably be a very helpful step toward humanity for them. I also like to imagine the wyrd and the principal as being great cosmological entities pressing against each other, a little bit like the triat from old world of darkness, so that can possibly be worth a couple plot hooks.<br /> <br /> Sin eaters would probably get on just fine with the changelings, they'd probably have a very similar deal as with werewolves, only with ghosts. gravewrights and the contracts of shade and spirit would probably synergize really well with the sin eaters. also, I don't recall for sure whether the hedge has a twilight side and if that forces ghosts and spirits that enter it to manifest, but the geists might appreciate having the option to interact with at least that part of the world directly rather than vicariously through the sin eater.<br /> <br /> Mummies I can't think of too much for, save for the entertaining confusion that would spring from them trying to figure out tokens. The local mummy would probably be the one the changelings give any props they recover from arcadia, seeing as he's sitting on a bunch of powerful magical artifacts to guard anyway and has a cult devoted to keeping them safe. you might also be able to explore some interesting interactions between the changeling's understanding of the Wyrd and a mummy's understanding of Fate.<br /> <br /> Demons would probably take a little while to get used to the idea that changelings can bind an agreement without writing it down. changelings would probably take a while to get used to demons being able to have as many contracts as they want (and, if they find out, the idea that demons can obliterate a soul with one). Probably the thing demons would find most interesting about changelings is the idea of a freehold. They have free agencies of their own, which actually seem very similar to freeholds thematically, but the interesting thing about how changelings do it is that they have an ordered system that, by the nature of its organization, achieves a specific effect (making it harder for fairies to enter and stay in your domain). This would probably look a lot like infrastructure to a demon, and more to the point it's an infrastructure that pushes back at the godly entities that were once the changeling's masters. I figure a lot of demons would take interest in that idea, perhaps exploring the possibility of adapting the system for use against the god machine and creating a comfortable little slice of hell for themselves. Also, I tend to see the god machine and the wyrd coming into conflict with each other (and the principal) like I mentioned above.<br /> <br /> as for the Z-splat thing, the differing flavor texts behind all the different Z-splats makes it hard to imagine all of them being part of one organization but I could easily see them being formed in concert with one another and being tied closely enough together that they essentially function as the same organization. Actually that would probably be pretty awesome, and any hunter conspiracy that forms from that union would probably get some really interesting options considering how many sources it would have to draw from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":807,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","user":"ArcadianAwakened","date":".  forgot the Z-splat and sin eaters 04-16-2014, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}